<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>Iris Quad (emap)</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>TerraLink emap</name>
    <email>software.guild@smail.iitm.ac.in</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    Quadrotor airframe geometry (base_link + 4 rotor links/joints) taken from the
    open-source 3DR Iris model in PX4/PX4-SITL_gazebo-classic (models/iris/iris.sdf.jinja,
    BSD-3-Clause). Meshes (iris.stl, iris_prop_ccw.dae, iris_prop_cw.dae) are vendored
    unmodified from that project.

    The PX4/Gazebo-Classic plugins (mavlink interface, PX4 motor model, sensors) from the
    original file were NOT carried over - they depend on Gazebo Classic and a PX4 SITL
    link. Instead this model is flown using Ignition Gazebo's native multicopter plugins
    (MulticopterMotorModel / MulticopterVelocityControl / OdometryPublisher), attached at
    include time in emap's world file, so the airframe works standalone under
    Ignition Gazebo Fortress + ros_gz.
  </description>
</model>
